  "result": "Fixed it. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:32` was matching lines by the item's name instead of its SKU. `'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so nothing was ever removed. It now matches on `l.item.sku`.\n\n- **Demo:** `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1` (only Gadget is left). Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- **Tests:** No existing test covered `remove`, so I added one in `tests/test_models.py`. pytest isn't installed, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest`: all 7 tests pass (the 6 existing ones plus the new one).",
